it took Karen Thomas three grueling  weeks and a lifetime of hard work to win  the Tour de France in a few seconds an  opportunist thief stole his glittering  prize Team Sky had loaned the coop Omni  Spore to bike maker Pinarello for the  cycle show in Birmingham organizers say  it had been momentarily left unattended  during the clear up afterwards Pinarello  say they accept full responsibility and  have personally apologized to Thomas in  a statement the Welsh cyclist said it is  incredibly unfortunate that this has  happened it goes without saying that the  trophy is of pretty limited value to  whoever took it but means a lot to me  and to the team hopefully whoever took  it will have the good grace to return us  this isn't the first time a major  sporting trophy has been stolen famously  before the 1966 World Cup in England the  Jules Rimet trophy went missing only to  be found by pickles the dog and it's not  just sporting memorabilia that attracts  thieves  this man is due to stand trial accused  of stealing Frances McDormand Oscar for  Best Actress at an after-party in Los  Angeles in March so why would anyone  want to take something that will be so  difficult to sell on it is quite  recognizable and certainly within the  sort of cycling world and so you  wouldn't be able to tell very many  people about it you certainly wouldn't  be able to have it on you on your  mantelpiece and sort of brag about it  but then again we know that there are  people that's still very very famous  artworks or have very famous artwork  stolen to order and just knowing they've  got them even if they've got to keep  them locked away somewhere that's enough  for some people Karen Thomas has urged  the thief to do the right thing and hand  it back he says no matter what happens  now nobody can ever take away the memory  of actually winning the Tour de France  and de Brady Sky News
 

